00:58:17,142 --> 00:58:23,142
Love, Rosie is a 2014 romantic comedy-drama film directed by Christian Ditter from a screenplay by
Juliette Towhidi, based on the 2004 novel Where Rainbows End by Irish author Cecelia Ahern.

13
01:03:08,571 --> 01:03:14,571
It stars Lily Collins and Sam Claflin as two childhood best friends turned lovers who
are separated by circumstances following their high school graduation.

14
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Christian Cooke, Tamsin Egerton, Suki Waterhouse, Jamie Beamish
and Jaime Winstone also appear in supporting roles.

15
01:12:51,428 --> 01:12:57,428
The film addresses themes such as teen pregnancy, adoption, grief and adultery.

16
01:17:42,857 --> 01:17:48,857
Love, Rosie had its world premiere in London on 6 October 2014,
before its theatrical release on 22 October 2014.

17
01:22:34,285 --> 01:22:40,285
Though the film was received poorly by critics, it garnered positive
reviews from audiences and grossed $25.5 million worldwide.

18
01:27:25,714 --> 01:27:31,714
Collins' performance was singled out for praise by both critics and audiences.

19
01:32:17,142 --> 01:32:23,142
